=== E8 as a rank-4 Hermitian lattice over O_F, F = Q(sqrt(-7)) (paper 4, eq. (7)) ===
H_E = [[2, 3, -3*sqrt(7)*I/7, -2*sqrt(7)*I/7], [3, 5, -5*sqrt(7)*I/7, -3*sqrt(7)*I/7], [3*sqrt(7)*I/7, 5*sqrt(7)*I/7, 1, 0], [2*sqrt(7)*I/7, 3*sqrt(7)*I/7, 0, 1]]
det H_E = 1/49  (Hermitian: True )
trace-form Gram (8x8): [[4, 2, 6, 3, 0, -3, 0, -2], [2, 8, 3, 12, 3, 0, 2, 0], [6, 3, 10, 5, 0, -5, 0, -3], [3, 12, 5, 20, 5, 0, 3, 0], [0, 3, 0, 5, 2, 1, 0, 0], [-3, 0, -5, 0, 1, 4, 0, 0], [0, 2, 0, 3, 0, 0, 2, 1], [-2, 0, -3, 0, 0, 0, 1, 4]]
integral: True  even diagonal: True  det = 1
vector counts by norm (<=4): {0: 1, 2: 240, 4: 2160} -> E8 has 240 roots, 2160 norm-4 vectors

=== Schur identity 7A - R R^T = I2 ===
7A - RR^T = [[1, 0], [0, 1]]  det R = -1
(I2 + R R^T) = 7A : True   -> top-left block of H_E is A; off-diagonal block R/sqrt(-7) not in O_F (lies in inverse different)

=== Gal(Q(zeta35)/Q(sqrt(-7))) ===
k with (k/7)=1: [1, 2, 4, 8, 9, 11, 16, 18, 22, 23, 29, 32]  size 12  matches paper 3 list: True
order of 2 mod 35: 12 -> subgroup cyclic of order 12 generated by 2: True
-1 mod 35 in subgroup? False  (so paper 4's description '(Z/35)^x/{+-1,+-2,...}' is not this subgroup)
zeta7+zeta7^2+zeta7^4 = (-0.5000000000000002+1.3228756555322954j)  vs w-1 = (-1+sqrt(-7))/2 = (-0.5+1.3228756555322954j)  equal: True
P(y) coefficients numerically: [(1+0j), (0.5-1.322875655532j), (-0.5-1.322875655532j), (-1+0j)]  expected [1, 1-w, -w, -1] = [1, (0.5-1.3228756555322954j), (-0.5-1.3228756555322954j), -1]

=== Lagrangian (maximal isotropic) subspace counts: brute force over small fields ===
q=3, dim 2m=4: hyperbolic quadratic: 8 Lagrangians (formula prod_(i=0..m-1)(q^i+1) = 8); fraction through a fixed singular vector = 1/4 (1/(q^(m-1)+1) = 1/4); symplectic: 40 (prod_(i=1..m)(q^i+1) = 40)
q=7, dim 2m=4: hyperbolic quadratic: 16 Lagrangians (formula prod_(i=0..m-1)(q^i+1) = 16); fraction through a fixed singular vector = 1/8 (1/(q^(m-1)+1) = 1/8); symplectic: 400 (prod_(i=1..m)(q^i+1) = 400)
q=3, dim 2m=6: hyperbolic quadratic: 80 Lagrangians (formula prod_(i=0..m-1)(q^i+1) = 80); fraction through a fixed singular vector = 1/10 (1/(q^(m-1)+1) = 1/10); symplectic: 1120 (prod_(i=1..m)(q^i+1) = 1120)
q=5, dim 2m=6: hyperbolic quadratic: 312 Lagrangians (formula prod_(i=0..m-1)(q^i+1) = 312); fraction through a fixed singular vector = 1/26 (1/(q^(m-1)+1) = 1/26); symplectic: 19656 (prod_(i=1..m)(q^i+1) = 19656)

=== numbers in paper 4, Section 4 ===
paper's N_Lag = prod_(i=1..24)(7^i+1) = 3.9596e+253  (symplectic count)
correct count for the hyperbolic quadratic space O+(48,7): prod_(i=0..23)(7^i+1) = 4.1336e+233; ratio = (7^24+1)/2 = 9.5791e+19
P(fixed isotropic line lies in random Lagrangian) = 1/(7^23+1) = 3.6538e-20  (paper uses 1/(7^24+1) = 5.2197e-21)
Gaussian heuristic #vectors of norm <= 4 in a 96-dim lattice of det 7^-48: 8.923e+11
Gaussian heuristic #vectors of norm <= 8 in a 96-dim lattice of det 7^-48: 2.512e+26
=> expected # norm<=8 vectors surviving a random Lagrangian gluing ~ 1.31e+6 (isotropic fraction ~1/7, inclusion prob 1/(7^23+1)); Siegel average (E_48) of norm-8 vectors in II_96 = 1.573e7, norm-6 = 21.1
paper's union bound 1e12/(7^24+1) = 5.220e-09; the 1e12 matches the Gaussian count at norm <= 4, not <= 8
